# VeloPhi supplement to the aqueous network (26.64, D267): the acid-base indicators as species of their own, so that an
# indicator takes part in the equilibrium like any weak acid and its colour changes continuously through the transition
# range. PHREEQC syntax, read by scripts/chem/build_aqueous.py after supplement.dat (every supplement_*.dat is).
#
# Each indicator is an element of its own. The master species is the base form; the acid forms are defined by log_k
# (cumulative protonation constants, as PHREEQC wants them). All values at 25 °C and ionic strength zero unless said
# otherwise, and all typed by hand from the references below ("hand" in docs/chem/DATA_SOURCES.md).
#
# Compositions for the LIGAND table of build_aqueous.py (the composition of the master species without its charge) —
# without these entries the generator drops the species; the lines are written so that they can be pasted:
#
#   'Phph': {'C': 20, 'H': 12, 'O': 4},
#   'Thph': {'C': 28, 'H': 29, 'O': 4},
#   'Meor': {'C': 14, 'H': 14, 'N': 3, 'O': 3, 'S': 1},
#   'Mered': {'C': 15, 'H': 14, 'N': 3, 'O': 2},
#   'Btb': {'C': 27, 'H': 26, 'Br': 2, 'O': 5, 'S': 1},
#   'Bcg': {'C': 21, 'H': 12, 'Br': 4, 'O': 5, 'S': 1},
#   'Phred': {'C': 19, 'H': 12, 'O': 5, 'S': 1},
#   'Thyb': {'C': 27, 'H': 28, 'O': 5, 'S': 1},
#   'Litmus': {'C': 12, 'H': 6, 'N': 1, 'O': 3},
#   'Alyr': {'C': 13, 'H': 7, 'N': 3, 'O': 5},
#   'Congo': {'C': 32, 'H': 22, 'N': 6, 'O': 6, 'S': 2},
#
# The lines "@indicator" are read by scripts/chem/check_reactions.py and by tests/chem/reactions.test.ts: the pKa of
# the step (log_k of the species with `step` protons minus that of the species with one proton fewer) must lie inside
# the textbook transition range written next to it. acid and base name the colours of the two forms of the step.
#
# References
#   KOLTHOFF  I. M. Kolthoff: Acid-Base Indicators (transl. C. Rosenblum), Macmillan, New York 1937: indicator
#             constants extrapolated to ionic strength zero (thymol blue 1.65 and 9.20, methyl orange 3.46,
#             bromocresol green 4.90, methyl red 5.00, bromothymol blue 7.30, phenol red 8.00), 20 to 25 °C; as
#             reproduced in R. G. Bates, Determination of pH, 2nd ed., Wiley 1973.
#   SABNIS    R. W. Sabnis: Handbook of Acid-Base Indicators, CRC Press, Boca Raton 2007: transition ranges, colours,
#             pKa of thymolphthalein, alizarin yellow R and congo red.
#   CRC       CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, 97th ed. (2016), section 8, "Acid-Base Indicators": transition
#             ranges and colours.
#   PHPH      The two close steps of phenolphthalein (pKa 9.05 and 9.50; a third, about 12, is the slow fading to the
#             colourless carbinol in strong alkali, which is kinetic and not modelled) as quoted in the secondary
#             literature (the article "Phenolphthalein" of Wikipedia and several data sheets, read 2026-11-14); the
#             primary source was not read. Not corrected to ionic strength zero.
#   YAMADA    Yamada's universal indicator (Japanese patent 99664, 1933), as given by L. S. Foster and I. J. Gruntfest,
#             J. Chem. Educ. 14, 274 (1937) and in the lecture-demonstration sheet of the University of Illinois
#             (read 2026-11-14): 0.005 g thymol blue, 0.012 g methyl red, 0.060 g bromothymol blue and 0.100 g
#             phenolphthalein in 100 mL of ethanol, neutralised to green with sodium hydroxide solution and diluted
#             to 200 mL with water.
#
# The universal indicator is not a species: it is a reagent whose recipe holds four of the indicators below. Per litre
# of Yamada's solution (the amounts above times five):
#     thymol blue        0.025 g  (466.59 g/mol)  5.36e-5 mol   as Na+ + H(Thyb)-
#     methyl red         0.060 g  (269.30 g/mol)  2.23e-4 mol   as H(Mered)
#     bromothymol blue   0.300 g  (624.38 g/mol)  4.80e-4 mol   as Na+ + H(Btb)-
#     phenolphthalein    0.500 g  (318.32 g/mol)  1.57e-3 mol   as H2(Phph)
# in water with half its volume of ethanol (the ethanol is an inert solute here). Colours: red (pH below 4), orange,
# yellow (6), green (7), blue (9 to 10), violet (above 10).
#
# What is simplified, and flagged in the @indicator lines:
#   flag=effective   one effective proton stands for a transition that is not a single step in reality:
#                    thymolphthalein (the real blue form is the dianion; its two steps are not resolved in the
#                    literature read) and litmus (a mixture of polymeric dyes; composition given as its chromophore
#                    7-hydroxyphenoxazone, pKa as the middle of the transition range).
#   The strongly acid forms of the sulfonephthaleins other than thymol blue (pKa about 1 or below), the second
#   protonation of methyl red (pKa about 2.3) and the carboxyl group of alizarin yellow R are left out: these
#   indicators are not used there.

SOLUTION_MASTER_SPECIES
Phph		Phph-2		0	316.31	316.31
Thph		Thph-		0	429.54	429.54
Meor		Meor-		0	304.34	304.34
Mered		Mered-		0	268.30	268.30
Btb		Btb-2		0	622.37	622.37
Bcg		Bcg-2		0	696.00	696.00
Phred		Phred-2		0	352.36	352.36
Thyb		Thyb-2		0	464.58	464.58
Litmus		Litmus-		0	212.18	212.18
Alyr		Alyr-2		0	285.22	285.22
Congo		Congo-2		0	650.68	650.68

SOLUTION_SPECIES
Phph-2 = Phph-2
Thph- = Thph-
Meor- = Meor-
Mered- = Mered-
Btb-2 = Btb-2
Bcg-2 = Bcg-2
Phred-2 = Phred-2
Thyb-2 = Thyb-2
Litmus- = Litmus-
Alyr-2 = Alyr-2
Congo-2 = Congo-2

# Phenolphthalein, C20H14O4: colourless lactone H2In and HIn-, pink dianion In2- (PHPH, hand)
# @indicator element=Phph name=phenolphthalein step=1 pKa=9.50 range=8.2..10.0 acid=colourless base=pink
# @indicator element=Phph name=phenolphthalein step=2 pKa=9.05 range=8.2..10.0 acid=colourless base=colourless
Phph-2 + H+ = H(Phph)-
	log_k	9.50
Phph-2 + 2 H+ = H2(Phph)
	log_k	18.55

# Thymolphthalein, C28H30O4: colourless below, blue above; pKa 9.9 (SABNIS, hand)
# @indicator element=Thph name=thymolphthalein step=1 pKa=9.9 range=9.3..10.5 acid=colourless base=blue flag=effective
Thph- + H+ = H(Thph)
	log_k	9.9

# Methyl orange, sodium salt C14H14N3NaO3S: red zwitterion HIn, yellow anion In-; pKa 3.46 (KOLTHOFF, hand)
# @indicator element=Meor name=methyl_orange step=1 pKa=3.46 range=3.1..4.4 acid=red base=yellow
Meor- + H+ = H(Meor)
	log_k	3.46

# Methyl red, C15H15N3O2: red HIn, yellow In-; pKa 5.00 (KOLTHOFF, hand)
# @indicator element=Mered name=methyl_red step=1 pKa=5.00 range=4.4..6.2 acid=red base=yellow
Mered- + H+ = H(Mered)
	log_k	5.00

# Bromothymol blue, C27H28Br2O5S: yellow HIn-, blue In2-; pKa 7.30 (KOLTHOFF, hand)
# @indicator element=Btb name=bromothymol_blue step=1 pKa=7.30 range=6.0..7.6 acid=yellow base=blue
Btb-2 + H+ = H(Btb)-
	log_k	7.30

# Bromocresol green, C21H14Br4O5S: yellow HIn-, blue In2-; pKa 4.90 (KOLTHOFF, hand)
# @indicator element=Bcg name=bromocresol_green step=1 pKa=4.90 range=3.8..5.4 acid=yellow base=blue
Bcg-2 + H+ = H(Bcg)-
	log_k	4.90

# Phenol red, C19H14O5S: yellow HIn-, red In2-; pKa 8.00 (KOLTHOFF, hand)
# @indicator element=Phred name=phenol_red step=1 pKa=8.00 range=6.8..8.4 acid=yellow base=red
Phred-2 + H+ = H(Phred)-
	log_k	8.00

# Thymol blue, C27H30O5S, two steps: red H2In, yellow HIn-, blue In2-; pKa 1.65 and 9.20 (KOLTHOFF, hand)
# @indicator element=Thyb name=thymol_blue step=1 pKa=9.20 range=8.0..9.6 acid=yellow base=blue
# @indicator element=Thyb name=thymol_blue step=2 pKa=1.65 range=1.2..2.8 acid=red base=yellow
Thyb-2 + H+ = H(Thyb)-
	log_k	9.20
Thyb-2 + 2 H+ = H2(Thyb)
	log_k	10.85

# Litmus (azolitmin): red below, blue above; one effective step in the middle of the range 5.0 to 8.0 (CRC, hand)
# @indicator element=Litmus name=litmus step=1 pKa=6.5 range=5.0..8.0 acid=red base=blue flag=effective
Litmus- + H+ = H(Litmus)
	log_k	6.5

# Alizarin yellow R, C13H9N3O5: yellow HIn-, red In2- (the phenol group); pKa 11.2 (SABNIS, hand)
# @indicator element=Alyr name=alizarin_yellow_R step=1 pKa=11.2 range=10.1..12.0 acid=yellow base=red
Alyr-2 + H+ = H(Alyr)-
	log_k	11.2

# Congo red, disodium salt C32H22N6Na2O6S2: blue-violet HIn-, red In2-; pKa 4.1 (SABNIS, hand)
# @indicator element=Congo name=congo_red step=1 pKa=4.1 range=3.0..5.0 acid=blue base=red
Congo-2 + H+ = H(Congo)-
	log_k	4.1
END
